    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6aa40dbc-c45b-58db-b883-b42884c67291",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "What is the order of the ordinary differential equation ${x}^{9}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3x=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{7}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{7}}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The order of an ordinary differential equation (ODE) is the order of the highest derivative in the equation.\n\nThe highest derivative in the given ODE is $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{7}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{7}},$ which has order $7.$\n\nTherefore, the order of the ODE is $7.$",
